{"title":"2005 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 23","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> be a diameter of a circle and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be a point on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/6/d66012ff3add95592a7adf808785b1d19b0157af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\cdot AC = BC$\" width=\"103\" height=\"13\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be points on the circle such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/1/831a6714862377b53fa5b94a7c71656ef314c6c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{DC} \\perp \\overline{AB}$\" width=\"82\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/9/699784c989c3db382520e6f92819e062d239f504.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{DE}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> is a second diameter. What is the ratio of the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/5/8c5425baeec765203a664dc6bd0f0562f2bf485a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DCE$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> to the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/5/f75d6d58b03031bd7cb52a7ca886a8ddf369d21c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/0/cb0ec00bcfe88917a6048c2cc4aaab8088e8872f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(2.5cm); defaultpen(fontsize(10pt)+linewidth(.8pt)); dotfactor=3; pair O=(0,0), C=(-1/3,0), B=(1,0), A=(-1,0); pair D=dir(aCos(C.x)), E=(-D.x,-D.y); draw(A--B--D--cycle); draw(D--E--C); draw(unitcircle,white); drawline(D,C); dot(O); clip(unitcircle); draw(unitcircle); label(&quot;$E$&quot;,E,SSE); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,E); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,W); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,NNW); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,SW); draw(rightanglemark(D,C,B,2));[/asy]\" width=\"272\" height=\"262\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/7/6176ed4dcbb1e12a8106aaf3ac71150cfebc83fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } \\frac{1}{6}\\qquad \\textbf{(B) } \\frac{1}{4}\\qquad \\textbf{(C) } \\frac{1}{3}\\qquad \\textbf{(D) } \\frac{1}{2}\\qquad \\textbf{(E) } \\frac{2}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"375\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Circlenc1.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/8/83/Circlenc1.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"279\" height=\"279\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p><p>WLOG, let us assume that the diameter is of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>The length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1965f8d70832ded66434c75a7bd52b75090af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/d/e9dc4f9abdac55c081c747fd2db62ae369497f05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CO$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/9/719f584734f05be763275a9169640467578ded2f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{3} = \\frac{1}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"84\" height=\"37\" />. \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/5/46569d6dd3fa86f698827e8de15b0480e1733d11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> is the radius of the circle, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />, so using the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_Theorem\" title=\"Pythagorean Theorem\">Pythagorean Theorem</a> the height <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/d/18d87922337210a9ecb2522803950fde46fe69ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DCO$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/d/39d05579b5f848e2574349ec54c612f736210d2f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^2-\\left(\\frac{1}{6}\\right)^2} = \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"184\" height=\"53\" />. This is also the height of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/5/f75d6d58b03031bd7cb52a7ca886a8ddf369d21c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>The area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/d/18d87922337210a9ecb2522803950fde46fe69ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DCO$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/0/cf09528e2b2a3412fceab4ab4edf9afd6546aa10.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"79\" height=\"41\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/3/0a3001352ca396a013508a45c7a0cf00411e89df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{36}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"26\" height=\"41\" />.\n</p><p>The height of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/5/8c5425baeec765203a664dc6bd0f0562f2bf485a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DCE$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> can be found using the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/d/18d87922337210a9ecb2522803950fde46fe69ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DCO$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/f/7ff1d53900652da5f2d40ef5427512642e85c0b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DO$\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" /> as base.\n</p><p>Hence, the height of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/5/8c5425baeec765203a664dc6bd0f0562f2bf485a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DCE$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/5/0d592c8be70c09aea04202effed539c8547adee9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{36}}{\\dfrac{1}{2}\\cdot\\dfrac{1}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -34px\" width=\"41\" height=\"82\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/d/67d2c9c921d1858b0e8dc8a0168bf9c39faf928a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"26\" height=\"41\" />. \n</p><p>The diameter is the base for both the triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/5/8c5425baeec765203a664dc6bd0f0562f2bf485a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DCE$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/5/f75d6d58b03031bd7cb52a7ca886a8ddf369d21c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" />,\n</p><p>Hence, the ratio of the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/5/8c5425baeec765203a664dc6bd0f0562f2bf485a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DCE$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> to the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/5/f75d6d58b03031bd7cb52a7ca886a8ddf369d21c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" /> is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/a/2ea4fb5a30f95d27a006a1d43017e239997540a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{9}}{\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -39px\" width=\"30\" height=\"87\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/5/6456cefcb4a5262eee52eda1b544496a5efc20d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) }\\frac{1}{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"59\" height=\"48\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/5/8c5425baeec765203a664dc6bd0f0562f2bf485a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DCE$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/5/f75d6d58b03031bd7cb52a7ca886a8ddf369d21c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" /> share a base, the ratio of their areas is the ratio of their altitudes. Draw the altitude from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/5/6d5c9afa92ae3180f02754c177e530d9d0f8b4d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/9/5e9629039a8bbef0413de3c19a864acbdb600acc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import graph; import olympiad; pair O,A,B,C,D,E,F; O=(0,0);A=(15,0);B=(-15,0);C=(5,0);D=(5,14.142135623730950488016887242097);E=(-5,-14.142135623730950488016887242097);F=(0.5555555555555555,1.5713484026367722764463208046774); draw(Circle((0,0),15));  draw(A--B);draw(D--E);draw(C--D);draw(C--E);draw(C--F);draw(A--D);draw(D--B); label(&quot;A&quot;,A,NE);label(&quot;B&quot;,B,W);label(&quot;C&quot;,C,SE);label(&quot;D&quot;,D,NE);label(&quot;E&quot;,E,SW);label(&quot;O&quot;,O,SW);label(&quot;F&quot;,F,NW); markscalefactor=0.2; draw(anglemark(C,F,D),blue);draw(anglemark(D,C,B),blue); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"238\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/c/23cb15c9ddc0b61dbf3f2b4121d33487ad3f9fb7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OD=r, OC=\\frac{1}{3}r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"144\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/5/c2585362857dc78fcf98ba7f5aa2d3fba0a83018.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\angle DCO=m\\angle DFC=90^\\circ$\" width=\"218\" height=\"13\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/4/8e400de3f243372cde8593edd3c769d039c9f4c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DCO\\sim \\triangle DFC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"147\" height=\"18\" />. So the ratio of the two altitudes is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/d/72d45ac2989b253c77f4cfc3f19a81161fd4cfd1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{CF}{DC}=\\frac{OC}{DO}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) }\\frac{1}{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"177\" height=\"49\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the center of the circle be point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />;\nWithout loss of generality, assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/d/53d084de05e313a40923ec33ee357544b1b93874.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC=2$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/f/d6fc685aa58768a47afbf7fd01c50cbd2dfc73fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CB=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"62\" height=\"13\" /> and the diameter and radius are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, respectively. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/e/4eed1e217bb14b892389f5ef8f60042aadba382e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CO=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/4/eb465295205ac8c083b62c7acd58fe47323dabd6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DO=3$\" width=\"62\" height=\"12\" />.\nThe area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/5/8c5425baeec765203a664dc6bd0f0562f2bf485a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DCE$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/9/ab9fdf49119b985ef4e1bed9aa7ed2caaea7e654.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}(CD)(6)\\text{sin }(CDE).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"172\" height=\"38\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092c577cd60014f96b82e82b49430ac1871b50f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}(CD)(6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"78\" height=\"37\" /> happens to be the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/5/f75d6d58b03031bd7cb52a7ca886a8ddf369d21c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" />. Furthermore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/0/7b03b77177cbed6632ea19252b2da73e974ddcf0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{sin } CDE = \\frac{CO}{DO},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"132\" height=\"37\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/d/6ad977fcc7b4a30cccb2941d091f5f051566b110.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"16\" height=\"37\" /> Therefore, the ratio is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/6/566b6fe3538f1ba1fd77816fc24ee9c620cfb6ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) }\\frac{1}{3}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"66\" height=\"49\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/3/d4350c278972068aa00c47f368b984efb308fff2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(2.5cm); defaultpen(fontsize(10pt)+linewidth(.8pt)); dotfactor=3; pair O=(0,0), C=(-1/3.0), B=(1,0), A=(-1,0); pair D=dir(aCos(C.x)), E=(-D.x,-D.y); draw(A--B--D--cycle); draw(D--E--C); draw(unitcircle,white); drawline(D,C); dot(O); clip(unitcircle); draw(unitcircle); label(&quot;$E$&quot;,E,SSE); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,E); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,W); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,NNW); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,SW); draw(rightanglemark(D,C,B,2)); [/asy]\" width=\"272\" height=\"262\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p>Let the point G be the reflection of point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> across <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />. (Point G is on the circle).\n</p><p><br />\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/4/2345cf4f7dddab7e3fbb69f1266183fce6d5d1be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC=x$\" width=\"62\" height=\"13\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/5/b456135c0b1ad89a495f98d7721d4eacdccc7b19.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=2x$\" width=\"72\" height=\"12\" />. The diameter is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/e/70e634348f8df9eaeac4ced35db64d08a906532e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />. To find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/e/27e525b776c49bbe7d0ae66cfc7ab8f58f40624e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />, there are two ways (presented here):\n</p><p>1. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> is the diameter, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/4/784f65f67919a93e579daa6b35aa994d0c7b85a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD=CG$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"85\" height=\"14\" />. Using power of points,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/3/723ade5bd214e9f80b53d8f81512d4d2ab40b2e2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AC\\cdot BC=x\\cdot2x=2x^{2}=CD^{2} \\longrightarrow CD=x\\sqrt{2}\\]\" width=\"378\" height=\"18\" />\n2. Use the geometric mean theorem,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/3/723ade5bd214e9f80b53d8f81512d4d2ab40b2e2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AC\\cdot BC=x\\cdot2x=2x^{2}=CD^{2} \\longrightarrow CD=x\\sqrt{2}\\]\" width=\"378\" height=\"18\" />\n(These are the same equations but obtained through different formulae)\n</p><p><br />\nTherefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/2/ce20e5df9095f58c9db43463874cfe7bd170dd77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DG=2x\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"98\" height=\"18\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/9/699784c989c3db382520e6f92819e062d239f504.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{DE}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> is a diameter, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/1/9c1b1ea9c8ebaa33d9a6480b52485e54ae998c0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DGE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" /> is right. By the Pythagorean theorem,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/a/caadf32b0b10a9f4bf3f585c0b33b1da0cf777c6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[DE^{2}=GD^{2}+GE^{2} \\longrightarrow \\left(3x\\right)^{2}=\\left(2x\\sqrt{2}\\right)^{2}+GE^{2}\\]\" width=\"391\" height=\"35\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/3/f535810c73ffe5cad5cfbab7691e5c738b09b0a1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[9x^{2}=8x^{2}+GE^{2} \\longrightarrow GE^{2}=x^{2} \\longrightarrow GE=x\\]\" width=\"356\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><br />\nAs established before, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/4/1d4679cc3f48dc4d1a567fc49514dd13c83a7ec3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle DGE$\" width=\"57\" height=\"12\" /> is right (if you are unsure, look up \"inscribed angle theorem\", this is a special case of the theorem where the central angle measures <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/0/3f0cd95f95238159d02dbcea0aca632c2928991c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"37\" height=\"15\" />) so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/6/f269c5510a2fc9f8890ad6289630d92ecb7dc691.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GE=x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"65\" height=\"14\" /> is the altitude of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/5/8c5425baeec765203a664dc6bd0f0562f2bf485a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DCE$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/1/8119ec74920f1b03bda562d0f43a14ccb55ba4a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DC=x\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"89\" height=\"18\" /> is the base. Therefore \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/4/4d41c053c8ddb6e0a29a677820c4b69bf5b38713.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left[DCE\\right]=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot DC\\cdot GE=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot x\\sqrt{2}\\cdot x=\\frac{x^{2}\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\]\" width=\"352\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/5/e55743cbd0cdc784ff68ee32d7f944d319489ab3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=3x$\" width=\"71\" height=\"13\" /> is the base of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/5/f75d6d58b03031bd7cb52a7ca886a8ddf369d21c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/9/3d9ea5e30078dc66d37550580e3e17a6c2195785.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD=x\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"91\" height=\"21\" /> is the height.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/b/5ebeeba7c5b92f11a0f207a4ca3887b2f866824b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left[ABD\\right]=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot3x\\cdot x\\sqrt{2}=\\frac{3x^{2}\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\]\" width=\"247\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p><br />\nThe required ratio is \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/d/12d0064aa10059252428b83f111593fed6081547.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\left[DCE\\right]}{\\left[ABD\\right]}=\\frac{\\frac{x^{2}\\sqrt{2}}{2}}{\\frac{3x^{2}\\sqrt{2}}{2}}=\\frac{x^{2}\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot\\frac{2}{3x^{2}\\sqrt{2}}=\\frac{x^{2}\\sqrt{2}}{3x^{2}\\sqrt{2}}=\\frac{1}{3}\\]\" width=\"380\" height=\"53\" />\nThe answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/3/553d5c27d65f56c6d4f6e548a4d2343d8d0d89df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) } \\frac{1}{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"59\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p>~JH. L\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Assume the diameter is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/6/5769bd8c4884b0688e98d67f254a7e3e2fa9f11f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>Get the height <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/b/a4b9604a00cf4c86ce14378aac5e273d72c4cb15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD = \\sqrt{(AC)(BC)} = \\sqrt2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"207\" height=\"35\" /> via power of a point.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/f/bbf0e50e4b2b26605db61a26ec6f8530cc47ccde.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CO = AO - AC = 1/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"184\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>By altitude of right triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/8/608f15d20377dddf3491a10e92479ffb6b14c43f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle CDO$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" />: Altitude from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/5/6d5c9afa92ae3180f02754c177e530d9d0f8b4d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> is same as altitude from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/f/7ff1d53900652da5f2d40ef5427512642e85c0b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DO$\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/a/67aa8ecf61a11eb1507d2f2243ce4cfc55c0fbef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{(CO)(CD)}{DO} = \\frac{(1/2)(\\sqrt2)}{\\frac 3 2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"201\" height=\"50\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/5/8c5425baeec765203a664dc6bd0f0562f2bf485a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DCE$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/5/f75d6d58b03031bd7cb52a7ca886a8ddf369d21c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" /> have the same (diameter) hypotenuse length, so their area ratio is their altitude ratio is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/8/fc85448652b9a5626c97b3de22d341e0806c7332.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {\\frac{ (1/2)(\\sqrt2) } {\\frac 3 2}} {\\sqrt2} = \\boxed{1/3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"131\" height=\"55\" />.\n</p><p>~oinava\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6\">Solution 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Think about <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/5/6d5c9afa92ae3180f02754c177e530d9d0f8b4d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> intersecting at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />. Now we realize that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/3/38367986004b4f309f112265ced1340d34398a9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XA = XB = XE = XD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"199\" height=\"14\" /> (this distance is just the radius of the circle), so that means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is the center.\n</p><p>So this can help us conclude that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/5/9057d4d264f5530ac63d366089bc3c17ce5d79a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABE$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/8/e08af8f3acc34996e3cba566dc970b7ed496ba4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ADB$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> are right triangles, and since it’s a rectangle setup, by Side-Angle-Side they are similar:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/5/ad59e0cd5c1e3fb303cc706a3682cdf7bbb4001a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABE \\sim \\triangle ADB.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"150\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>So because of this, the altitudes of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/5/8c5425baeec765203a664dc6bd0f0562f2bf485a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DCE$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/5/9057d4d264f5530ac63d366089bc3c17ce5d79a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABE$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/8/e08af8f3acc34996e3cba566dc970b7ed496ba4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ADB$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> are the same (with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> as the altitude). Hence we need to find the ratio\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/1/5f1397ef049b7d2657696229e5e6b2409ce60004.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2CX}{AB}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"51\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/1/7f158b2d15494baef20cc8217f53ead695896f1a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AC:CB = 1:2 \\Rightarrow \\quad AX:XB = 1:1 \\Rightarrow AC:CX = 2:1.\\]\" width=\"471\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/2/b92645d2afa9b73689389c524ba35dcf5c740402.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC:CB = 1:2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"131\" height=\"14\" />, it follows that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/5/ed54c41352e227bbb6f99399c312c685c900b8a5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[BX:CX = 1:4 \\Rightarrow CX:AB = 1:6.\\]\" width=\"297\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>Therefore,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/9/96992a12ffe38d97713332dfa83072d841623dd6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{2CX}{AB} = 2 \\cdot \\frac{1}{6} = \\boxed{\\frac{1}{3}}\\]\" width=\"150\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p>~~ Randomuser456 (I need help on the latex...)\n~LQS (latex)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_solution\">Video solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/i6eooSSJF64\">https://youtu.be/i6eooSSJF64</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A\">2005 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki